# Server

# Firebase emulators (Auth + Firestore + Storage) — FILLED IN ON PURPOSE. Treat the four as
# one block: fill them all or empty them all.
# As shipped: `pnpm emulators` + `pnpm seed` + `pnpm dev` runs the whole stack locally,
# offline, with no Google account and without touching real data — and the service
# account below becomes unnecessary.
# To use a REAL Firebase project, EMPTY all four (VAR="") and fill in the service
# account. Running the emulators needs a JDK 21+ runtime. See docs/SETUP.md.
FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:8080"
FIREBASE_AUTH_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:9099"
# With it, uploads go to the Storage emulator under the demo bucket, whatever
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET says. Emptied while the two hosts above stay filled in, uploads
# stay switched off (STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED) rather than reaching a real bucket.
FIREBASE_STORAGE_EMULATOR_HOST="127.0.0.1:9199"
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="demo-next-boilerplate"

# Firebase service account — required when the emulator hosts above are empty. It is how
# the API authenticates to Firestore (its database) and to Firebase Auth.
# Keep the newlines in the private key escaped as \n.
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PROJECT_ID=""
FIREBASE_ADMIN_CLIENT_EMAIL=""
FIREBASE_ADMIN_PRIVATE_KEY=""

# Firebase Web API key — the API calls the Identity Toolkit REST endpoints with it
# (the account lookup of the GitHub sign-in, and the password change).
# Found under Project settings > General > Web API Key.
FIREBASE_WEB_API_KEY=""

# Cloud Storage bucket (e.g. "my-project.firebasestorage.app"). OPTIONAL: without it the
# upload capability stays switched off — POST /files answers STORAGE_NOT_CONFIGURED and
# the panel shows the photo URL field instead of the file picker. Falls back to
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET when empty.
# Filling it in requires the Firebase Blaze plan, i.e. a payment method on file: Cloud
# Storage does not exist on Spark, where every call to a bucket answers 402/403. Real
# spend is still $0/month at MVP scale. Create the bucket in us-central1, us-east1 or
# us-west1 — they are the only regions with a free tier. See docs/PRE-PRODUCTION.md.
# Ignored while the emulator hosts above are filled in: uploads go to the Storage
# emulator, and an emulated stack never writes into a real bucket.
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=""

# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed to call the API. REQUIRED in
# production: the process refuses to start without it. Left empty outside production,
# the local panel below is assumed. There is no wildcard.
CORS_ORIGIN="http://localhost:3000"

# Optional. Without it, @repo/security degrades to a no-op: the public auth routes
# accept unlimited requests and the API says so once, at boot.
# The value must start with "ajkey_": anything else is treated as absent and the API
# logs an error at boot.
ARCJET_KEY=""

# GitHub App of the board. OPTIONAL until production: without these three the API still
# starts, POST /github/webhook answers GITHUB_APP_NOT_CONFIGURED and, while the emulator
# hosts above are filled in, the API uses sample repositories instead of GitHub.
# The App id is numeric. Keep the newlines in the private key escaped as \n.
# See docs/PRE-PRODUCTION.md.
GITHUB_APP_ID=""
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=""
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# Key that seals the scheduled task credentials (fire URL and token) of each member: 32
# random bytes in base64, e.g. `openssl rand -base64 32`. OPTIONAL: without it the API
# still starts, saving a scheduled task answers CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_NOT_CONFIGURED and
# the credentials page shows the cloud section switched off. While FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST
# is filled in, an emulator-only key is used instead. Changing the key makes every stored
# scheduled task unreadable. See docs/PRE-PRODUCTION.md.
CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL="http://localhost:3002"

# Client
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=""
# Public host of apps/app.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Brand (optional; neutral defaults when empty). Public values, inlined at build:
# changing them needs a new deploy. The logo must be an absolute, public http(s) URL
# of a square mark.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_LOGO_URL=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_SUPPORT_EMAIL=""

# Absolute session lifetime in days. Leave empty for the default (30). Must match the
# value of apps/app.
SESSION_ABSOLUTE_MAX_AGE_DAYS=""
